  The Firecracker release bundle includes libseccomp which is available
  under the LGPLv2.1 license. This is used in the Firecracker build process
  to produce cBPF bytecode that is shipped alongside Firecracker for use by
  the Linux kernel.

crates/compat/ contains builds of rust-vmm crates (vm-memory, event-manager,
vhost, kvm-bindings, kvm-ioctls, vmm-sys-util), libc, memfd, userfaultfd and
micro_http. Each keeps its upstream license, stated in its Cargo.toml; the
sources under crates/compat/*/src/windows/ are generated from the upstream
crate by the scripts in tools/.
